  "lineage": "Songs of the Big Drum religion (Drum Dance or Dream Dance), which spread from the Dakota to the Ojibwe, Menominee and Potawatomi of Wisconsin and Minnesota from the late nineteenth century, after the vision in which a Dakota woman was given the drum. Each consecrated drum, a large drum suspended from four curved, decorated legs, has its own members, offices and songs, sung by the drummers seated around it during seasonal ceremonies. The powwow drum card stands in for the dance drum.",
